  "query_preview": "(This evening through Sunday)...\nIssued at 301 PM EDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nRounds of surface high pressure will continue to bring dry weather \nand mostly clear skies throughout the week. Highs are expected to \nremain slightly above normal for this time of year while lows \nwill start off slightly below normal and become near normal by \nmidweek. \n\nTemperatures tonight are again expected to drop into the 30s, but \nshould stay in the mid to upper 30s range as more southerly flow \ntoday will help keep conditions slightly warmer than last night. \nStill expecting patchy to widespread frost across the forecast area \ntonight, especially in low lying areas so have another frost \nadvisory from 2am to 9am. Lows the rest of the week should stay in \nthe 40s so not expecting the need for additional headlines at this \ntime. \n\nModel soundings show persistent dry air through the column so most \ndays throughout the week should see largely clear skies or only a \nfew clouds. Chances for some clouds increase towards the end of the \nweek/ weekend when the upper pattern becomes a bit more amplified \nand may bring in slightly more moisture. \n\nThere is some concern of worsening drought conditions and fire \nweather this week given the lack of precipitation. Daily minimum RH \nvalues will range from low 30 percentiles to around 50%. Luckily \nwinds will not be much of a concern, but do take precautions with\nany open fires.",
